# Tests for the Ptc_allowed module (Form 8962 lines 9 to 25)

Run with `clerk test`. Named scopes with the concrete cases of issue #33,
worked out by hand from IRC 36B(b) and (c) and the Instructions for Form 8962
(2024) (`sources/forms-instructions/i8962--2024.pdf`: line 10 p 12 to 13,
line 11 p 13 to 14, lines 12 to 23 p 14 to 15, lines 24 and 25 p 15). Oracle
comparison: `make difftest SCOPE=ptc_allowed`.

> Using Types
> Using Ptc_allowed as A

## Helpers

```catala-metadata
## `amount` in months `first` to `last` (1 to 12), $0 in the others.
declaration amounts_in content list of money
  depends on
    first content integer,
    last content integer,
    amount content money
  equals
    map each m among (List.sequence of 1, 13) to
      (if first <= m and m <= last then amount else $0)

## The month numbers `first` to `last`.
declaration months_between content list of integer
  depends on
    first content integer,
    last content integer
  equals
    List.sequence of first, (last + 1)

## A 1095-A for the whole of 2024 with no change: DF asks the line 33
## annual amounts.
declaration full_year_form content A.Form1095A
  depends on
    annual_premium content money,
    annual_slcsp content money,
    annual_aptc content money
  equals
    A.Form1095A {
      -- writable_policy_start_date: |2024-01-01|
      -- writable_policy_end_date: |2024-12-31|
      -- writable_special_policy_modification_in_starting_month: false
      -- writable_has_policy_date_exception: false
      -- has_coverage_months: true
      -- coverage_months: months_between of 1, 12
      -- writable_premiums_or_slcsp_change: false
      -- has_change_in_circumstance: false
      -- writable_ptc_annual_premium: annual_premium
      -- writable_slcsp_annual_premium: annual_slcsp
      -- writable_aptc_annual_amount: annual_aptc
      -- writable_ptc_monthly_premium: amounts_in of 1, 12, $0
      -- writable_ptc_monthly_slcsp_premium: amounts_in of 1, 12, $0
      -- writable_ptc_monthly_aptc_premium: amounts_in of 1, 12, $0
    }

## A 1095-A from `start` to `ends`, coverage months `first` to `last`, with
## the same monthly amounts in those months: DF asks the monthly amounts.
declaration part_year_form content A.Form1095A
  depends on
    start content date,
    ends content date,
    first content integer,
    last content integer,
    premium content money,
    slcsp content money,
    aptc content money
  equals
    A.Form1095A {
      -- writable_policy_start_date: start
      -- writable_policy_end_date: ends
      -- writable_special_policy_modification_in_starting_month: false
      -- writable_has_policy_date_exception: false
      -- has_coverage_months: true
      -- coverage_months: months_between of first, last
      -- writable_premiums_or_slcsp_change: false
      -- has_change_in_circumstance: false
      -- writable_ptc_annual_premium: $0
      -- writable_slcsp_annual_premium: $0
      -- writable_aptc_annual_amount: $0
      -- writable_ptc_monthly_premium: amounts_in of first, last, premium
      -- writable_ptc_monthly_slcsp_premium: amounts_in of first, last, slcsp
      -- writable_ptc_monthly_aptc_premium: amounts_in of first, last, aptc
    }
```

By default: a single applicable taxpayer at 200 percent of the poverty line
with a qualifying plan, no APTC, a contribution amount of $1,200 a year
(line 8a) and $100 a month (line 8b), one full-year Form 1095-A with $8,000 of
premiums and a $7,200 SLCSP, and every knockout question answered no. A test
overrides only what it tests.

```catala
declaration scope Case:
  context filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  context forms content list of A.Form1095A
  context has_aptc condition
  context percent content decimal
  context annual_contribution content money
  context monthly_contribution content money
  context mfs_exception condition
  context below100_immigration_exception condition
  context married condition
  context qsehra condition
  context employer_plan condition
  context multiple_1095_as condition
  context wants_alt_calculation condition
  a scope A.PtcAllowed
  output annual_path condition
  output allowed content money
  output aptc content money
  output annual_allowed content money
  output applicable condition
  output needs_8962 condition
  output months content list of A.PtcMonth
  output unsupported condition
  output ko_multiple condition

scope Case:
  definition filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition forms equals [full_year_form of $8,000, $7,200, $0]
  definition percent equals 200.0
  definition annual_contribution equals $1,200
  definition monthly_contribution equals $100

  definition a.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition a.is_mfj_dependent equals false
  definition a.not_mfj_and_primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits equals false
  definition a.primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent equals false
  definition a.is_married equals married
  definition a.secondary_filer_residency_eligible_for_mfj equals true
  definition a.lived_apart_last_six_months equals false
  definition a.all_eligible_filers_are_us_citizens_or_nationals equals true
  definition a.claimed_dependents_count equals 0
  definition a.has_qsehra equals qsehra
  definition a.household_income_as_percent equals percent
  definition a.ptc_annual_contribution_amount equals annual_contribution
  definition a.ptc_monthly_contribution_amount equals monthly_contribution
  definition a.form1095_as equals forms
  definition a.writable_has_ptc_qualifying_plan equals true
  definition a.writable_has_advanced_ptc equals has_aptc
  definition a.dependent_tp_self_enrolled equals false
  definition a.dependent_tp_enrolled_someone_else equals false
  definition a.writable_dependent_tp_other_members_are_part_of_different_tax_family equals false
  definition a.writable_has_mfs_exception equals mfs_exception
  definition a.writable_claiming_mfs_exception_for_fourth_straight_year equals false
  definition a.writable_below100_threshold_and_not_eligible_for_medicaid_because_of_immigration_status
    equals below100_immigration_exception
  definition a.writable_has_employer_sponsored_plan equals employer_plan
  definition a.writable_dependents_required_to_file equals false
  definition a.writable_self_reported_has_multiple1095_as equals multiple_1095_as
  definition a.writable_is_additional_person_in_enrollment_family equals false
  definition a.writable_is_additional_person_partof_different_tax_family equals false
  definition a.writable_is_enrolled_with_other_family equals false
  definition a.writable_has_immigration_status_not_eligible_for_marketplace equals false
  definition a.writable_wants_to_use_alt_calculations equals wants_alt_calculation

  rule annual_path under condition a.ptc_can_report_annual_totals consequence fulfilled
  definition allowed equals a.total_ptc_amount_allowed
  definition aptc equals a.total_aptc_amount_taken
  definition annual_allowed equals a.annual_ptc_allowed
  rule applicable under condition a.potentially_applicable_tax_payer consequence fulfilled
  rule needs_8962 under condition a.needs_to_file_form8962 consequence fulfilled
  definition months equals a.ptc_months
  rule unsupported under condition a.unsupported consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_multiple under condition a.ko_tp_needs_to_delete1095_a consequence fulfilled
```

## Line 11: a 12-month policy uses the annual path

Full year, no change: line 10 "Yes". Line 11(d) = $7,200 - $1,200 = $6,000;
line 11(e) = lesser of $8,000 and $6,000 = $6,000. A bad output (the SLCSP,
the premium, or the monthly path's amount) is rejected.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestTwelveMonthPolicyAnnualPath:
  c scope Case

scope TestTwelveMonthPolicyAnnualPath:
  assertion c.annual_path
  assertion c.needs_8962
  assertion c.allowed = $6,000
  assertion c.annual_allowed = $6,000
  assertion c.aptc = $0
  assertion c.allowed != $7,200
  assertion c.allowed != $8,000
  assertion not c.unsupported
```

## Lines 12 to 23: a policy starting in July

July 1 to December 31: six coverage months, monthly path. Each month: (b)
$600 - (c) $100 = (d) $500; (e) lesser of (a) $500 and $500 = $500; six
months give $3,000. APTC of $50 a month gives line 25 = $300. January to June
are blank ($0).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestJulyStartMonthlyPath:
  c scope Case

scope TestJulyStartMonthlyPath:
  definition c.has_aptc equals true
  definition c.forms equals
    [part_year_form of |2024-07-01|, |2024-12-31|, 7, 12, $500, $600, $50]
  assertion not c.annual_path
  assertion c.allowed = $3,000
  assertion c.aptc = $300
  assertion c.allowed != $6,000
  assertion (number of (list of r among c.months such that r.ptc_allowed > $0)) = 6
  assertion (number of (list of r among c.months such that r.contribution_amount > $0)) = 6
  assertion exists r among c.months such that
    r.month_number = 7 and r.enrollment_premium = $500 and r.slcsp_premium = $600
    and r.contribution_amount = $100 and r.max_premium_assistance = $500
    and r.ptc_allowed = $500 and r.advance_payment = $50
  assertion exists r among c.months such that
    r.month_number = 6 and r.enrollment_premium = $0 and r.ptc_allowed = $0
    and not r.has_active_policy
```

## Two Forms 1095-A

January to June in one state ($400 premium, $450 SLCSP), July to December in
another ($300 premium, $500 SLCSP); line 10 "No" since neither is full year.
January to June: lesser of $400 and $450 - $100 = $350, six months $2,100.
July to December: lesser of $300 and $400 = $300, six months $1,800. Line 24
= $3,900. Direct File refuses two forms (`/tpNeedsToDelete1095A`), so the
return is unsupported.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestTwo1095As:
  c scope Case

scope TestTwo1095As:
  definition c.forms equals
    [part_year_form of |2024-01-01|, |2024-06-30|, 1, 6, $400, $450, $0;
     part_year_form of |2024-07-01|, |2024-12-31|, 7, 12, $300, $500, $0]
  assertion not c.annual_path
  assertion c.allowed = $3,900
  assertion c.allowed != $2,100
  assertion c.ko_multiple
  assertion c.unsupported
```

## Column (d) below zero

SLCSP $600 a year, contribution $1,200: line 11(d) "If the result is zero or
less, enter -0-", so nothing is allowed, never a negative amount.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSlcspBelowContributionAllowsNothing:
  c scope Case

scope TestSlcspBelowContributionAllowsNothing:
  definition c.forms equals [full_year_form of $8,000, $600, $0]
  assertion c.annual_path
  assertion c.allowed = $0
  assertion c.allowed != -$600
```

Monthly: a $90 SLCSP against a $100 contribution gives $0 for the month.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMonthlySlcspBelowContribution:
  c scope Case

scope TestMonthlySlcspBelowContribution:
  definition c.forms equals
    [part_year_form of |2024-03-01|, |2024-05-31|, 3, 5, $500, $90, $0]
  assertion c.allowed = $0
  assertion c.allowed != -$30
```

## Allowed amount capped by the premium

Premium $4,000 a year, SLCSP $7,200: lesser of $4,000 and $6,000 = $4,000
(IRC 36B(b)(2)(A)).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestAllowedCappedByPremium:
  c scope Case

scope TestAllowedCappedByPremium:
  definition c.forms equals [full_year_form of $4,000, $7,200, $0]
  assertion c.allowed = $4,000
  assertion c.allowed != $6,000
```

## Annual APTC and rounding

APTC of $2,400.60 reported for the year: line 25 is $2,401 (whole dollars).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestAnnualAptcRounded:
  c scope Case

scope TestAnnualAptcRounded:
  definition c.has_aptc equals true
  definition c.forms equals [full_year_form of $8,000, $7,200, $2,400.60]
  assertion c.annual_path
  assertion c.allowed = $6,000
  assertion c.aptc = $2,401
```

## DF-BUG(31): a policy starting on December 1

Covered on December 1, so December is a coverage month (IRC 36B(c)(2)(A)(i)):
lesser of $500 and $600 - $100 = $500. Direct File gives $0.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDecemberFirstStartIsCoverageMonth:
  c scope Case

scope TestDecemberFirstStartIsCoverageMonth:
  definition c.forms equals
    [part_year_form of |2024-12-01|, |2024-12-31|, 12, 12, $500, $600, $0]
  assertion c.allowed = $500
  assertion c.allowed != $0
```

A policy starting on December 15 (no birth or adoption exception) has no
coverage month.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMidDecemberStartNoCoverageMonth:
  c scope Case

scope TestMidDecemberStartNoCoverageMonth:
  definition c.forms equals
    [part_year_form of |2024-12-15|, |2024-12-31|, 12, 12, $500, $600, $0]
  assertion c.allowed = $0
```

## Policy-date exception (26 CFR 1.36B-3(c)(2))

A policy starting on March 15 for a newborn, with the exception claimed:
March counts. Without the exception it does not.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPolicyDateExceptionCountsStartMonth:
  c scope Case

scope TestPolicyDateExceptionCountsStartMonth:
  definition c.forms equals
    [A.Form1095A {
       -- writable_policy_start_date: |2024-03-15|
       -- writable_policy_end_date: |2024-04-30|
       -- writable_special_policy_modification_in_starting_month: true
       -- writable_has_policy_date_exception: true
       -- has_coverage_months: true
       -- coverage_months: [3; 4]
       -- writable_premiums_or_slcsp_change: false
       -- has_change_in_circumstance: false
       -- writable_ptc_annual_premium: $0
       -- writable_slcsp_annual_premium: $0
       -- writable_aptc_annual_amount: $0
       -- writable_ptc_monthly_premium: amounts_in of 3, 4, $500
       -- writable_ptc_monthly_slcsp_premium: amounts_in of 3, 4, $600
       -- writable_ptc_monthly_aptc_premium: amounts_in of 3, 4, $0
     }]
  assertion c.allowed = $1,000

#[test]
declaration scope TestMidMonthStartWithoutException:
  c scope Case

scope TestMidMonthStartWithoutException:
  definition c.forms equals
    [part_year_form of |2024-03-15|, |2024-04-30|, 3, 4, $500, $600, $0]
  assertion c.allowed = $500
  assertion c.allowed != $1,000
```

## DF-BUG(32): full-year policy with 11 coverage months

A policy from January 20 to December 31 with no exception and no change: DF
asks the annual amounts and uses line 11, allowing $6,000. January is not a
coverage month (not covered on January 1), so the monthly path is used:
eleven months of lesser of $8,000 / 12 = $666.67 and $600 - $100 = $500,
that is $5,500.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFullYearPolicyWithElevenCoverageMonths:
  c scope Case

scope TestFullYearPolicyWithElevenCoverageMonths:
  definition c.forms equals
    [A.Form1095A {
       -- writable_policy_start_date: |2024-01-20|
       -- writable_policy_end_date: |2024-12-31|
       -- writable_special_policy_modification_in_starting_month: false
       -- writable_has_policy_date_exception: false
       -- has_coverage_months: true
       -- coverage_months: months_between of 1, 12
       -- writable_premiums_or_slcsp_change: false
       -- has_change_in_circumstance: false
       -- writable_ptc_annual_premium: $8,000
       -- writable_slcsp_annual_premium: $7,200
       -- writable_aptc_annual_amount: $0
       -- writable_ptc_monthly_premium: amounts_in of 1, 12, $0
       -- writable_ptc_monthly_slcsp_premium: amounts_in of 1, 12, $0
       -- writable_ptc_monthly_aptc_premium: amounts_in of 1, 12, $0
     }]
  assertion not c.annual_path
  assertion c.allowed = $5,500
  assertion c.allowed != $6,000
```

## Who may claim the credit

Married filing separately without the domestic abuse or abandonment
exception: not an applicable taxpayer (IRC 36B(c)(1)(C)). Line 24 is $0 and
all the APTC is repaid (i8962 p 14, "Not an applicable taxpayer").

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfsWithoutExceptionRepaysAllAptc:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfsWithoutExceptionRepaysAllAptc:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition c.married equals true
  definition c.has_aptc equals true
  definition c.forms equals [full_year_form of $8,000, $7,200, $3,000]
  assertion not c.applicable
  assertion c.needs_8962
  assertion c.allowed = $0
  assertion c.aptc = $3,000
  assertion c.allowed != $6,000

#[test]
declaration scope TestMfsWithExceptionIsApplicable:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfsWithExceptionIsApplicable:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition c.married equals true
  definition c.mfs_exception equals true
  assertion c.applicable
  assertion c.allowed = $6,000
```

Below 100 percent of the poverty line with no APTC and no immigration-status
exception: not applicable, no Form 8962. With APTC paid, 26 CFR
1.36B-2(b)(6) keeps the taxpayer applicable.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestBelowPovertyLineNoAptcNotApplicable:
  c scope Case

scope TestBelowPovertyLineNoAptcNotApplicable:
  definition c.percent equals 90.0
  definition c.annual_contribution equals $0
  definition c.monthly_contribution equals $0
  assertion not c.applicable
  assertion not c.needs_8962
  assertion c.allowed = $0

#[test]
declaration scope TestBelowPovertyLineWithAptcApplicable:
  c scope Case

scope TestBelowPovertyLineWithAptcApplicable:
  definition c.percent equals 90.0
  definition c.annual_contribution equals $0
  definition c.monthly_contribution equals $0
  definition c.has_aptc equals true
  definition c.forms equals [full_year_form of $8,000, $7,200, $7,000]
  assertion c.applicable
  assertion c.allowed = $7,200
  assertion c.aptc = $7,000
```

## Knockouts

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestQsehraKnockedOut:
  c scope Case

scope TestQsehraKnockedOut:
  definition c.qsehra equals true
  assertion c.unsupported

#[test]
declaration scope TestEmployerPlanKnockedOut:
  c scope Case

scope TestEmployerPlanKnockedOut:
  definition c.employer_plan equals true
  assertion c.unsupported

#[test]
declaration scope TestSelfReportedMultipleKnockedOut:
  c scope Case

scope TestSelfReportedMultipleKnockedOut:
  definition c.multiple_1095_as equals true
  assertion c.unsupported
```

The alternative calculation for year of marriage is asked only of a married
couple filing jointly with excess APTC.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestAltCalculationKnockedOut:
  c scope Case

scope TestAltCalculationKnockedOut:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.married equals true
  definition c.has_aptc equals true
  definition c.wants_alt_calculation equals true
  definition c.forms equals [full_year_form of $8,000, $7,200, $7,000]
  assertion c.unsupported

#[test]
declaration scope TestAltCalculationNotAskedWithoutExcessAptc:
  c scope Case

scope TestAltCalculationNotAskedWithoutExcessAptc:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.married equals true
  definition c.has_aptc equals true
  definition c.wants_alt_calculation equals true
  definition c.forms equals [full_year_form of $8,000, $7,200, $5,000]
  assertion not c.unsupported
```
